  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> be the relation defined on the set of all real numbers such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "symmetric and transitive but not reflexive",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "reflexive and transitive but not symmetric",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "an equivalence relation",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>its reflexive relation.</p><p>Now&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mfenced><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math><br /><br />Hence, it is symmetric.<br /><br />If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><mi>sec</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8658;</mo></math> transitive&nbsp;<br /><br />So, it is an equivalence relation.</p>"
  }
